    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "sometimes i just sit in my living room and it feels like i'm watching a movie of someone else's life. i spent thirty years in the OR, every second mattered, every move had a purpose. now i just... wake up, drink coffee, and wait for the day to end. it's like the person i actually was died when i hung up the scrubs, and this thing left behind is just a ghost. it feels so pointless.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's completely normal to feel this way, transitioning from a high-intensity job to a more relaxed lifestyle. Remember, taking the time to care for your mental and physical well-being can help you reconnect with aspects of yourself that may feel lost. Also, exploring new hobbies or volunteering can bring a feeling of purpose and fulfillment. It's not too late to discover who you are outside of your career.",
      "source": "target",
